74
00:03:37,130 --> 00:03:38,290
Mornin', Allen.

75
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:41,420
Good morning, head servant, sir!

76
00:03:41,670 --> 00:03:43,290
Aw, just call me Rickel.

77
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:44,380
All right.

78
00:03:44,710 --> 00:03:47,830
So, are you getting along well with Lady Cecil?

79
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,960
Uh, yeah...

80
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:52,420
Sorta...

81
00:03:52,790 --> 00:03:53,790
I see.

82
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:56,080
I can hear the pity in his voice...

83
00:03:56,580 --> 00:03:58,040
Well, that's life as a manservant for you.

84
00:03:58,170 --> 00:04:01,960
She wouldn't demand as much
if you were only a hallboy.

85
00:04:02,170 --> 00:04:04,580
Actually, I've been meaning to ask.

86
00:04:04,580 --> 00:04:07,330
What exactly is the difference
between hallboy and manservant?

87
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:09,830
Oh, has nobody told you yet?

88
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:15,670
The senior rank servants include: butler,
housekeeper, valet, lady-in-waiting, head chef.

89
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:21,710
And the lower ranks are: coachman,
cook, gardener, manservant, housemaid.

90
00:04:17,290 --> 00:04:24,130
Notes on the Gravelles:

91
00:04:17,290 --> 00:04:24,130
High rank servants:

92
00:04:17,290 --> 00:04:24,130
Butler, housekeeper, valet,

93
00:04:17,290 --> 00:04:24,130
lady-in-waiting, head chef.

94
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:24,130
Low rank servants:

95
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:24,130
Coachman, cook, gardener,

96
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:24,130
manservant, housemaid.

97
00:04:21,710 --> 00:04:23,920
All of those are formally
considered part of the family.

98
00:04:24,130 --> 00:04:28,580
Hallboys are only helpers,

99
00:04:24,130 --> 00:04:28,580
so they are not part of the family.

100
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:26,920
But hallboys are only occasional helpers,

101
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:28,580
so they don't count as being
a member of the family.

102
00:04:28,750 --> 00:04:30,000
Wait, family?

103
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,080
Servants are members of the family itself?

104
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:33,170
Yeah, of course.

105
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:38,210
Holy crap. No wonder Dad was crying tears of joy.

106
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:42,580
The baron was generous enough
to make me part of the family.

107
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,630
Gotta be grateful for that.

108
00:04:47,130 --> 00:04:49,790
I wasn't surprised by the
simple meals we servants get,

109
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:52,080
but I guess the nobility
doesn't eat much better, huh?

110
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:54,580
I wonder if the baron
is one of those frugal types.

111
00:04:57,540 --> 00:05:00,080
You've picked up the basics
of being a servant quickly, Allen.

112
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:04,330
Thank you, milady. I owe it all
to the kind teachings of my seniors.

113
00:05:04,460 --> 00:05:06,380
My! What a wonderful answer!

114
00:05:06,580 --> 00:05:10,290
His manners are beyond what you'd expect
of a serf, aren't they, dear?

115
00:05:10,630 --> 00:05:13,750
Indeed. And in spite of him being talentless.

116
00:05:14,170 --> 00:05:16,420
Huh? Did he do some digging on me?

117
00:05:16,790 --> 00:05:19,580
Oh my? You don't have a talent, Allen?

118
00:05:21,170 --> 00:05:22,380
Heh!

119
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:25,130
Well, I happen to be a Wizardess!

120
00:05:25,290 --> 00:05:26,540
Wizardess?

121
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:30,170
That's a two star talent. Pretty good.

122
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:33,380
And my elder brother Mihai is a Swordsman!

123
00:05:33,380 --> 00:05:33,960
Cecil!

124
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:38,880
How many times must I tell you?
Don't brag about talents.

125
00:05:42,330 --> 00:05:44,670
Why am I the only one without one...?

126
00:05:45,130 --> 00:05:46,920
Cheer up, Thomas.

127
00:05:47,290 --> 00:05:49,630
You will attend Nobles College
in the royal capital.

128
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:54,960
But I want to go to
the Academy City like Mihai did...

129
00:05:55,210 --> 00:05:56,330
I'm afraid you can't.

130
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,880
The Academy City is only for those with a talent.

131
00:06:00,170 --> 00:06:03,210
My lack of talent is why
I attended Nobles College, too.

132
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:06,210
But that's where I met your mom
and started our family.

133
00:06:06,670 --> 00:06:08,000
Don't let it bother you, Thomas.

134
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:09,380
Okay.

135
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,830
I'm sorry, Thomas...

136
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:15,880
Why do I get the stink eye?

137
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:20,170
Hey, Allen! You going out?

138
00:06:20,170 --> 00:06:22,170
Yes. I have the afternoon off today.

139
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:29,170
This place is a whole new world
compared to the village.

140
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:36,500
It's the Adventurer's Guild!

141
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:40,130
Pardon me, ma'am!

142
00:06:40,130 --> 00:06:42,420
Can I become an Adventurer?

143
00:06:42,580 --> 00:06:44,170
How old are you, young man?

144
00:06:44,170 --> 00:06:45,040
I'm eight!

145
00:06:45,290 --> 00:06:49,880
Well, I'm sorry. You have to be 12 or older
to register as an Adventurer.

146
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:52,000
No, say it ain't so!

147
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:55,420
I'm doing the whole manservant thing
out of respect for Dad,

148
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:58,130
but I refuse to give up on monster hunting!

149
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:01,040
