to search for them instead.

272
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:30,040
Summon five more!

273
00:10:31,580 --> 00:10:34,580
Use your Hawk Eye skill to find nearby monsters.

274
00:10:36,330 --> 00:10:40,210
Wow! It sure is handy having them
at my beck and call!

275
00:10:40,210 --> 00:10:42,130
Let's try it out with another creature.

276
00:10:42,420 --> 00:10:43,170
BEAST E

277
00:10:42,420 --> 00:10:43,170
BUFFS: HP+10, ATTACK+10

278
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:43,710
Tama, I choose you!

279
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:47,580
Okay, Tama. Come over here!

280
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:50,420
Huh?

281
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:55,330
RANK:

282
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:55,330
NAME:

283
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:55,330
TAMA

284
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:55,330
HP:

285
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:55,330
MP:

286
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:55,330
ATTACK:

287
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:55,330
ENDURANCE:

288
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:55,330
AGILITY:

289
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:55,330
INTELLIGENCE:

290
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:55,330
LUCK:

291
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:55,330
TYPE:

292
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:55,330
BEAST

293
00:10:51,830 --> 00:10:53,460
Guess it can't understand me

294
00:10:53,460 --> 00:10:55,080
with only 28 intelligence...

295
00:10:55,670 --> 00:10:56,790
Whatever.

296
00:10:57,130 --> 00:10:59,960
Well, Dogora. Time to put your gift to good use.

297
00:11:01,580 --> 00:11:03,250
Oh, did you find some?

298
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:05,130
Great!

299
00:11:07,710 --> 00:11:10,540
Come on, man. Where are the monsters?

300
00:11:11,750 --> 00:11:16,380
I'll have to make my orders more specific
next time. Like limiting them to a certain range.

301
00:11:24,330 --> 00:11:26,130
Finally, some action.

302
00:11:26,540 --> 00:11:28,080
Those must be goblins.

303
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:31,830
BEAST E

304
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:31,830
HP+10, ATTACK+10

305
00:11:31,170 --> 00:11:32,790
Summon: Tama! Five times!

306
00:11:36,670 --> 00:11:37,630
And that's not all...

307
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:39,330
Another five makes ten!

308
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:43,920
My creatures can be summoned to any location
that I can mark by sight within a 50 meter radius.

309
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:45,710
Tama! Use your claw attack!

310
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:51,630
Hell yeah! Easy-peasy!

311
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,460
Or not so much...

312
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:57,330
I haven't tested this one yet,
but I'm betting it works...

313
00:11:57,330 --> 00:11:58,170
INSECT E

314
00:11:57,330 --> 00:11:58,170
ENDURANCE+10, AGILITY+10

315
00:11:57,340 --> 00:11:58,630
Come on out, Papillon!

316
00:12:01,670 --> 00:12:05,420
Powdaa, powdaa, powdaa, powdaa, powdaa.

317
00:12:05,420 --> 00:12:08,460
I figured that powder ability
would put them to sleep!

318
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,580
That wasn't enough to kill it, huh?

319
00:12:18,630 --> 00:12:22,580
YOU HAVE DEFEATED 1 GOBLIN.

320
00:12:18,630 --> 00:12:22,580
YOU HAVE GAINED 200 EXP.

321
00:12:18,630 --> 00:12:22,580
YOU HAVE DEFEATED 1 GOBLIN.

322
00:12:18,630 --> 00:12:22,580
YOU HAVE GAINED 200 EXP.

323
00:12:18,630 --> 00:12:22,580
YOU HAVE DEFEATED 1 GOBLIN.

324
00:12:18,630 --> 00:12:22,580
YOU HAVE GAINED 200 EXP.

325
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:22,500
Yahoo! Defeating five of them earned me 1,000 EXP!

326
00:12:22,830 --> 00:12:24,750
Wicked sick!

327
00:12:25,290 --> 00:12:27,500
Efficiency is key when it comes to grinding EXP.

328
00:12:27,670 --> 00:12:30,330
Even though one goblin doesn't give
as much as a great boar,

329
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:34,080
they take less time to beat,
so it's a way better deal!

330
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:36,080
Now we're cooking with gas!

331
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:41,540
Hey, Hawkins! Find more goblins!

332
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:46,380
Let me know if you see a group of five or more
within a 3 kilometer radius of here.

333
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:55,040
Powdaa, powdaa, powdaa, powdaa.

334
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:03,830
Today I farmed: five horned rabbits
and eighty goblins.

335
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,960
That's 16,050 worth of EXP, baby!

336
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:09,330
I leveled up twice!

337
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:12,250
This is the best day off EVER!

338
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:17,210
I got some valuable data
on Papillon's debuff, too.

339
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:21,000
When used against goblins, it has about
an 80% chance of inducing sleep.

340
00:13:21,290 --> 00:13:25,250
It goes to show that even one summoned creature
can be useful against a hoard of monsters.

341
00:13:25,710 --> 00:13:28,040
I also learned a little about magic stones.

342
00:13:28,210 --> 00:13:31,920
D-rank magic stones can't be used
to create E-rank summon creatures.

343
00:13:32,130 --> 00:13:34,040
Naturally, the inverse doesn't work, either.

344
00:13:34,130 --> 00:13:39,330
D-RANK MAGIC STONES CAN'T BE USED

345
00:13:34,130 --> 00:13:39,330
TO CREATE E-RANK SUMMON CREATURES.

346
00:13:34,130 --> 00:13:39,330
THE INVERSE DOESN'T WORK, EITHER.

347
00:13:34,130 --> 00:13:39,330
BE MINDFUL THERE ARE SITUATIONS

348
00:13:34,130 --> 00:13:39,330
WHERE I MIGHT NEED

349
00:13:34,130 --> 00:13:39,330
MY LOWER RANK SUMMONS.

350
00:13:34,630 --> 00:13:38,920
I have to be mindful that there are situations
where I might need my lower rank summons.

351
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:40,130
Okay.

352
00:13:40,330 --> 00:13:42,830
The farming continues! Go, Hawkins!

353
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:48,080
What's the matter? The night is still young, guys!

354
00:13:49,670 --> 00:13:52,880
Huh? Wait... can you not see
at night or something?

355
00:13:53,540 --> 00:13:54,960
What are you, chickens?!

356
00:13:55,170 --> 00:13:56,460
Seriously?

357
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:59,080
I mean, I guess they're not owls...

358
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:04,080
Well, crap. I was counting on Hawkins
to help me find my way back to town later.

359
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:07,710
So, in other words, I'm lost in the woods...?

360
00:14:08,290 --> 00:14:10,960
HOW DO I GET HOME NOW?!

361
00:14:11,710 --> 00:14:13,960
MIRACULOUSLY FOUND HIS WAY BACK

362
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:17,960
THE HARDCORE GAMER DOMINATES

363
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:17,960
IN ANOTHER WORLD WITH GARBAGE BALANCING

364
00:14:18,170 --> 00:14:21,040
ONE MONTH LATER

365
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:22,000
Is this what had you had in mind for iron balls?

366
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:23,830
Yeah, they're perfect!

367
00:14:24,250 --> 00:14:26,920
It'll be 60 silver coins for the three.

368
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:27,670
Okay!

369
00:14:28,630 --> 00:14:31,250
I wanted something with more oomph
than rocks, so I ordered these.

370
00:14:31,250 --> 00:14:33,210
They should do some real damage!

371
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:36,880
I've gone monster hunting four more times
since then and now I'm level 12.

372
00:14:37,210 --> 00:14:40,790
Farming easy mobs for EXP
while collecting better equipment.

373
00:14:41,290 --> 00:14:43,710
The tried-and-true strategy for any game!

374
00:14:48,750 --> 00:14:49,580
Allen.

375
00:14:52,290 --> 00:14:53,920
We need to have a talk.

376
00:14:53,920 --> 00:14:54,540
Yessir...

377
00:14:56,500 --> 00:15:00,540
Allen. You have proved yourself a very capable
servant over the past two months.

378
00:15:01,170 --> 00:15:05,040
I've heard nothing but good things
about your work from both Sebas and Rickel.

379
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:06,500
Thank you, milord.

380
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:09,880
However, I must know what you've been doing
on your days off.

381
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:10,630
Huh?

382
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:14,420
You always leave bright and early,
yet return well after dark.

383
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:17,670
Naturally, you're free to spend your time off
however you wish.

384
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:19,830
But I want to keep abreast of your activities.

385
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:22,580
Yeah, it figures they'd get concerned.

386
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:25,420
I should be as honest as possible here.

387
00:15:26,210 --> 00:15:28,380
I've been hunting monsters
in the forests outside of town.

388
00:15:28,710 --> 00:15:31,330
Hm? Why would you do that?

389
00:15:31,750 --> 00:15:34,420
Because I'm the son of Rodin the Boar Hunter.

390
00:15:34,790 --> 00:15:36,830
Hunting runs in my blood, milord.

391
00:15:37,210 --> 00:15:39,250
Ah, I see.

392
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:44,170
Whoa. I just said that on impulse,
but it feels right.

393
00:15:44,540 --> 00:15:46,380
The apple never falls far from the tree, huh?

394
00:15:47,380 --> 00:15:50,500
Fair enough, Allen. You are the son of a legend.

395
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:52,830
I suppose you can't help what's in your nature.

396
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:57,000
So, what have you been doing
with the horned rabbits you hunt?

397
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,670
Hm? Horned rabbits?

398
00:15:59,170 --> 00:16:02,580
Oh, I get it. They think
I've been hunting E-rank monsters.

399
00:16:03,250 --> 00:16:06,960
If you've been selling their meat
to a butcher for money, then you must stop.

400
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:08,130
It could cause a scandal.

401
00:16:08,630 --> 00:16:09,790
Sorry, sir.

402
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,580
Actually, I've just been throwing it all away.

403
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:12,880
Instead...

404
00:16:13,670 --> 00:16:17,000
The Granvelle estate will purchase
that horned rabbit meat from you

405
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:18,880
for one silver coin per bundle.

406
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:19,960
What do you say?

407
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:21,380
Wow, really?

408
00:16:21,580 --> 00:16:25,630
This means I can hunt openly
AND make money off the meat!

409
00:16:26,040 --> 00:16:27,380
I gladly accept, thank you!

410
00:16:29,170 --> 00:16:32,460
SIX MONTHS LATER

411
00:16:30,330 --> 00:16:32,580
I want to farm at least 100 goblins today.

412
00:16:32,830 --> 00:16:36,460
And maybe some horned rabbits to get
more pocket money and magic stones.

413
00:16:36,750 --> 00:16:38,290
About five should do it.

414
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:44,710
Hey. Did you find goblins?
I'll go once I finish eating this.

415
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:49,710
What's wrong? You guys are acting weird.

416
00:16:50,170 --> 00:16:51,210
Okay, I'm coming!

417
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:56,000
They're moving so fast.
And leading me too far out.

418
00:16:56,380 --> 00:16:58,330
I told them within three kilometers!

419
00:17:03,210 --> 00:17:04,460
Run for it, Milci!

420
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:07,000
I can't! Not without you two!

421
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:07,790
Just do it!

422
00:17:08,330 --> 00:17:09,790
I'll hold them off!

423
00:17:17,420 --> 00:17:18,380
I'm here to help.

424
00:17:20,420 --> 00:17:23,000
Dammit! Iron balls aren't enough to kill them.

425
00:17:23,250 --> 00:17:25,210
I've seen these three
at the Adventurer's Guild before.

426
00:17:25,630 --> 00:17:27,960
That's a nasty cut. He's in trouble!

427
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:31,830
I can't use my summons in front of them.
It's time to get my hands dirty!

428
00:17:32,250 --> 00:17:33,920
You take the goblin with one hand.

429
00:17:34,170 --> 00:17:35,250
A-all right.

430
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:44,040
I'm currently level 12. And thanks to my
summon buffs, my attack and agility are over 300.

431
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:50,210
So I can take down D-rank monsters
even without my creatures.

432
00:17:50,670 --> 00:17:51,290
Next!

433
00:17:57,790 --> 00:17:58,750
Raven!

434
00:17:59,210 --> 00:18:01,750
He didn't surpass a Trial of the Gods...

435
00:18:01,750 --> 00:18:03,330
Then just heal him!

436
00:18:03,330 --> 00:18:06,540
I'm sorry, but... I don't have any MP left.

437
00:18:06,540 --> 00:18:07,670
Oh no!

438
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:10,130
C'mon, Raven! Don't die on me!

439
00:18:11,250 --> 00:18:13,330
He won't last the trip back to town.

440
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:15,710
I have some healing herbs that we can try.

441
00:18:16,460 --> 00:18:17,290
Really?!

442
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:20,420
We'll pay however much you want!
Please save Raven!

443
00:18:22,130 --> 00:18:23,670
This is a "Leaf of Life"

444
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:26,830
TYPE:

445
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:26,830
GRASS

446
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:26,830
RANK:

447
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:26,830
NAME:

448
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:26,830
HP:

449
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:26,830
MP:

450
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:26,830
ATTACK:

451
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:26,830
ENDURANCE:

452
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:26,830
AGILITY:

453
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:26,830
INTELLIGENCE:

454
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:26,830
LUCK:

455
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:26,830
BUFFS:

456
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:26,830
MP +10, LUCK +10

457
00:18:23,670 --> 00:18:25,080
that I made using Beanzie's ability.

458
00:18:25,460 --> 00:18:27,330
I'm pretty sure it heals HP, but...

459
00:18:39,630 --> 00:18:40,710
Raven!

460
00:18:41,540 --> 00:18:43,210
Thank heavens! You're okay!

461
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:45,790
Rita... Milci...

462
00:18:45,790 --> 00:18:47,130
Do you feel all right?

463
00:18:47,130 --> 00:18:48,130
Any pain?

464
00:18:48,420 --> 00:18:49,250
My wound...

465
00:18:49,250 --> 00:18:50,670
Glad you pulled through.

466
00:18:51,250 --> 00:18:52,130
It's you...

467
00:18:52,670 --> 00:18:54,710
Looks like you have a wound, too, Ms. Rita.

468
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:56,420
Let's take care of that.

469
00:18:58,210 --> 00:19:01,500
Is that a muellerze flower? Or some kinda leaf?

470
00:19:01,630 --> 00:19:04,130
Such a strong healing item
and you used two for us...

471
00:19:04,130 --> 00:19:05,830
Don't worry about it.

472
00:19:06,290 --> 00:19:08,130
It's not at all what they think.

473
00:19:08,670 --> 00:19:09,670
Thanks for saving us.

474
00:19:10,210 --> 00:19:13,670
You're the kid who I met
at the Adventurer's Guild... right?

475
00:19:14,420 --> 00:19:17,420
Yes. No need to worry about those injuries now.

476
00:19:17,750 --> 00:19:19,380
So, I'll just be on my way.

477
00:19:19,790 --> 00:19:22,670
Wait a second! At least let us repay you!

478
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,710
I owe you my life, kid!

479
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:29,580
Aw, jeez. I've gotta get back to farming
right away if I want to hit my goal for the day.

480
00:19:30,040 --> 00:19:32,580
Okay, then please don't tell anybody about me.

481
00:19:32,830 --> 00:19:35,330
Sure thing. Let us know
if there's anything else we can do.

482
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:38,580
Oh! Actually, I'm collecting magic stones.

483
00:19:38,790 --> 00:19:41,000
Could you gather 100 E-rank ones for me?

484
00:19:41,290 --> 00:19:43,290
I-is that really all you want?

485
00:19:43,460 --> 00:19:45,080
Yes, absolutely!

486
00:19:45,330 --> 00:19:47,580
Normies may not have any use for 'em,
but those magic stones

487
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:50,000
are valuable to Summoners like me!

488
00:19:50,290 --> 00:19:53,790
You got it. We'll have those ready for you
in about a week.

489
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:54,880
Bye-bye!

490
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,920
Thank you. Farewell!

491
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:55,250
See you around!

492
00:20:00,630 --> 00:20:05,210
It took about a month for Dad to fully recover
after they used the muellerze flower on him.

493
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:08,630
But Raven healed almost instantly
with that Leaf of Life.

494
00:20:09,420 --> 00:20:10,460
Which leads me to conclude...

495
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:15,250
The muellerze flower recovers
a certain amount of HP relative to the maximum.

496
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:17,080
It's a percentage-based healing item.

497
00:20:17,540 --> 00:20:21,040
Whereas the Leaf of Life
is a fixed-HP healing item.

498
00:20:21,670 --> 00:20:26,080
And what's more, I only earned 160 EXP
per goblin in that battle.

499
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:28,540
That's 80% of what I get when farming them solo.

500
00:20:28,750 --> 00:20:32,540
YOU HAVE DEFEATED 1 GOBLIN.

501
00:20:28,750 --> 00:20:32,540
YOU HAVE GAINED 160 EXP.

502
00:20:28,750 --> 00:20:32,540
YOU HAVE DEFEATED 1 GOBLIN.

503
00:20:28,750 --> 00:20:32,540
YOU HAVE GAINED 160 EXP.

504
00:20:28,750 --> 00:20:32,540
YOU HAVE DEFEATED 1 GOBLIN.

505
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:32,540
YOU HAVE GAINED 160 EXP.

506
00:20:29,170 --> 00:20:32,670
So EXP isn't divided by the number of people
when I defeat monsters in a party, huh?

507
00:20:33,290 --> 00:20:34,750
Now, for the biggest problem...

508
00:20:35,290 --> 00:20:36,580
Come on out, Hawkins!

509
00:20:40,170 --> 00:20:42,080
Why did you ignore my orders?

510
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:47,670
I told you to find a group of five or more goblins
within a three kilometer radius, didn't I?

511
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:53,420
Were you worried about those adventurers?
Did you want to save them?

512
00:20:56,250 --> 00:20:59,130
Oh wow. Are you actually sapient, buddy?

513
00:21:00,750 --> 00:21:03,830
I was under the impression my summons
were just for providing buffs,

514
00:21:03,830 --> 00:21:05,960
using abilities, and following orders.

515
00:21:06,130 --> 00:21:07,580
But there's more to it, huh?

516
00:21:08,920 --> 00:21:11,540
Hawkins prioritized its own feelings
over my orders,

517
00:21:11,750 --> 00:21:14,790
and led me to Raven's group
because it knew they were in trouble.

518
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:16,580
Hot damn.

519
00:21:17,630 --> 00:21:19,880
Elmea made amazing summon creatures.

520
00:21:21,330 --> 00:21:25,040
Sorry, Hawkins. I wasn't trying
to make you feel bad.

521
00:21:26,330 --> 00:21:29,960
I'll be more careful with my orders in the future,
in case something like this happens again.

522
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:32,250
I'm glad to have you on my team.

523
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:38,540
Go left more!

524
00:21:38,790 --> 00:21:40,630
Too far, dummy!

525
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:43,000
Why do you always suck so bad at this?

526
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:44,250
Well, excuse me.

527
00:21:44,580 --> 00:21:47,540
Hawkins, go dump her in a lake for me, would ya?

528
00:21:47,750 --> 00:21:52,000
If I may, milady,
what do you even need jam for...?

529
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:54,250
To help me bake yummy cookies.

530
00:21:54,250 --> 00:21:56,040
And that matters why, exactly?!

531
00:21:56,210 --> 00:22:00,330
Because my elder brother Mihai
is coming home next spring, silly.

532
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:01,710
Huh?

533
00:22:04,130 --> 00:22:05,710
Who did that?!

534
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:07,130
Meow!

535
00:22:07,130 --> 00:22:08,710
Oh, it's just the cat.

536
00:22:09,040 --> 00:22:10,210
Back to sleep...

